#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:20
msgid ""
"TOML selects reviewed modes and Board routes. The resolver checks fields, "
"capacities and conflicts, produces immutable typed IR and publishes one "
"atomic bundle. CMake remains the sole software target graph. Invalid input "
"neither selects a fallback mode nor leaves a usable partial configuration."
msgstr ""
"TOML selects reviewed modes and Board routes. The resolver checks fields, "
"capacities and conflicts, produces immutable typed IR and publishes one "
"atomic bundle. CMake remains the sole software target graph. Invalid input "
"neither selects a fallback mode nor leaves a usable partial configuration."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:25
msgid ""
"Factory lookup returns an existing static face; it does not allocate, read "
"silicon, initialize hardware or start tasks. Ordinary I/O dispatches through "
"shared readonly ops with the instance context. Applications own scheduling, "
"service progress and shutdown. Multiple faces do not create multiple owners "
"of the same physical controller."
msgstr ""
"Factory lookup returns an existing static face; it does not allocate, read "
"silicon, initialize hardware or start tasks. Ordinary I/O dispatches through "
"shared readonly ops with the instance context. Applications own scheduling, "
"service progress and shutdown. Multiple faces do not create multiple owners "
"of the same physical controller."

