#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:40
msgid ""
"These are build-time proofs about supplied facts. Runtime hardware withdrawal"
" still requires the concrete C implementation. Clock, reset, shared filter "
"and timer-domain dependencies remain held until their users can actually "
"exit."
msgstr ""
"These are build-time proofs about supplied facts. Runtime hardware withdrawal"
" still requires the concrete C implementation. Clock, reset, shared filter "
"and timer-domain dependencies remain held until their users can actually "
"exit."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:44
msgid "Bind stream budgets to actual storage"
msgstr "Bind stream budgets to actual storage"

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:46
msgid ""
"Selected continuous UART and ADC profiles bind declared rates, service bounds"
" and exact pools. Hardware targets, replacement blocks and consumer retention"
" must fit actual capacity and integer ranges. These declarations are "
"assumptions, not measured latency or a lossless guarantee."
msgstr ""
"Selected continuous UART and ADC profiles bind declared rates, service bounds"
" and exact pools. Hardware targets, replacement blocks and consumer retention"
" must fit actual capacity and integer ranges. These declarations are "
"assumptions, not measured latency or a lossless guarantee."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:51
msgid ""
"The application supplies all storage and joins pool users before "
"reconfiguration. A producer never overwrites READY or BORROWED blocks. If "
"replacement or service progress is insufficient it stops and reports loss. "
"Cancellation and timeout do not revoke a loan; failed drain preserves "
"quarantine and cleanup responsibility."
msgstr ""
"The application supplies all storage and joins pool users before "
"reconfiguration. A producer never overwrites READY or BORROWED blocks. If "
"replacement or service progress is insufficient it stops and reports loss. "
"Cancellation and timeout do not revoke a loan; failed drain preserves "
"quarantine and cleanup responsibility."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:56
msgid "Keep units and ownership explicit"
msgstr "Keep units and ownership explicit"

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:58
msgid ""
"UART uses bytes or the selected word format; ADC block counts use complete "
"scans; frames carry their reviewed layout and stride. Validate size "
"arithmetic, alignment and payload/control aliasing before retaining "
"references. DMA memory completion, peripheral wire completion and request "
"settlement are distinct."
msgstr ""
"UART uses bytes or the selected word format; ADC block counts use complete "
"scans; frames carry their reviewed layout and stride. Validate size "
"arithmetic, alignment and payload/control aliasing before retaining "
"references. DMA memory completion, peripheral wire completion and request "
"settlement are distinct."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:63
msgid ""
"Optional traits describe the selected implementation, not the chip's complete"
" marketing feature set. A controller, endpoint and companion interface retain"
" their own typed identities. Querying a capability does not prove "
"initialization, readiness, resource ownership or physical qualification."
msgstr ""
"Optional traits describe the selected implementation, not the chip's complete"
" marketing feature set. A controller, endpoint and companion interface retain"
" their own typed identities. Querying a capability does not prove "
"initialization, readiness, resource ownership or physical qualification."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:68
msgid "Validate one selected implementation"
msgstr "Validate one selected implementation"

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:70
msgid ""
"Tests execute the production C with external hardware boundaries modeled. "
"Exercise rejection, cancellation, overflow, late events, actual withdrawal, "
"instance isolation and error recovery. ARM linking checks the selected ABI, "
"vectors and real memory layout; SDK checks independent consumption."
msgstr ""
"Tests execute the production C with external hardware boundaries modeled. "
"Exercise rejection, cancellation, overflow, late events, actual withdrawal, "
"instance isolation and error recovery. ARM linking checks the selected ABI, "
"vectors and real memory layout; SDK checks independent consumption."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:75
msgid ""
"Measure resource changes under identical toolchain and configuration. "
"Physical IRQ latency, throughput, stack high-water and power require an "
"actual station. Unexecuted measurements stay unexecuted. The original cross-"
"family increments and ledgers retain their original evidence at [the fixed "
"prior source](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/tree/8e147fc2c812d81ab6596e0d1a6bc8908d30ac18/docs/design), without"
" becoming current F4 support claims."
msgstr ""
"Measure resource changes under identical toolchain and configuration. "
"Physical IRQ latency, throughput, stack high-water and power require an "
"actual station. Unexecuted measurements stay unexecuted. The original cross-"
"family increments and ledgers retain their original evidence at [the fixed "
"prior source](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/tree/8e147fc2c812d81ab6596e0d1a6bc8908d30ac18/docs/design), without"
" becoming current F4 support claims."
